( 6... Nb4? { Eyes c2, but one knight cannot do that alone, and it has left the centre to White. }
  7. e4 { Takes the centre and hits the bishop. }
  7... Bg6 8. Nf3 Nf6 9. a3 { The knight has to go back to where it came from. White has the centre and a big lead in time, and the engine puts that at more than two pawns. The gain is positional: no material has changed hands. } )
